	(text "16C550 UART ON THE CLOCK'S PORT PAIR, MAX232, DE-9" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9801941c-187f-5e9b-ae3b-5048d935f324"))
	(text "U20 16C550 (Ken, 2026-11-20; as on his YACC1 I/O card): X1 1.8432 MHz on XIN, -BAUDOUT to RCLK, MR = RESET_H, the\nmodem inputs tied off. It shares the clock's ports (JP4): U22 (LE = RTC_AS) holds the byte written to the address\nport: bit 7 = SEL_UART (1: the UART, CS0; 0: the DS12885, its CS), bits 2-0 = the UART's register. WR = RTC_WR, high in\nTPB of an OUT to the data port. -RD = UART_RD_L from U11B, preset by -MWR low (only an INP has it) and held clear while\nRTC_RD is low: the 1802 puts N out 1.5 clocks before -MRD falls in an OUT, so RTC_RD pulses at the start of every\nOUT to the data port, and a 16550 read there would throw a received character away. INTR through U9C (open\ncollector, RN1) and JP7 to -INT (off). U21 MAX232 with four 1 uF; JP6 swaps the DE-9's pins 2 and 3 (1-3 and 2-4:\nthe card sends on pin 2); J2's shell to GND." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "42c2d297-00b0-504f-b953-76f11a44a9f9"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
